column5:
I have a few shares, overall they hold nearly 1M files.

We're testing out the latest beta for the truesearch functionality.

Truesearch finished indexing, but searches take about 7 or 8 seconds, and the client (Finder) always timees out.

We already tried storing the index on SSD, and as a temporary test I also moved the index to a tmpfs in-memory filesystem.

Although that improved speed for the smaller share, the largest shares are still timing out.

I don't see any tunable knobs on truesearch that could help with this.

Here's the relevant part of the log for a specific search:

```
